            "target_entity_type": "Project",
            "paragraph": "Projections of future climates were grouped into near-term (NT) (2019-2048) and mid-century (MC) (2049\u20132078) simulations under moderate emissions of Shared Socioeconomic Pathways (SSP245) and high emissions (SSP585) climate scenarios. Climate change data under the SSP245 and SSP585 scenarios were extracted from the Coupled Model Intercomparison Project Phase 6 (CMIP6) archive. CMIP6 is the latest phase of CMIP, which aims to enhance the representation of emission scenarios and increase horizontal resolution, thereby making future projections more realistic 71,72. To incorporate bias-corrected and high-resolution (0.25\u00b0) projections, the study relied on Model for Interdisciplinary Research on Climate, version 6 (MIROC6) data processed through NASA's Earth Exchange Global Daily Downscaled Projections (NEX-GDDP) system 73. MIROC6 was selected based on a Compromise Programming Lp-metric ranking 74, as it performed best among 10 CMIP6 models in simulating precipitation (r > 0.82) and temperature (r > 0.64), while also effectively capturing teleconnections in the Ethiopian highlands 75. Climate data were averaged across all stations within each AES for the AES-level analyses.",
